question was optional. Lawfulness is affine, the landed family is
lawful at every t, fifteen of the ladder's rows never depended on
the choice, and the rows that do depend on something need only that
one value be avoided, not that one be picked. The backlog's three
strays are priced, one theorem comes out larger than its discoverer
